<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry of Flanders</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1176–<a href="/years/1216">1216</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> from 1205, succeeding his brother Baldwin I. He was the ablest of the Latin emperors, defending the empire against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a> and the Nicaeans and conciliating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>. In 1208–1209 he suppressed the revolt of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> barons of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-of-flanders.jpg" alt="Henry of Flanders" width="271" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Schlumberger, Gustave Léon, 1844-1929 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henry_Flandry.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…took the title Prince of Achaea, but when he left for France in 1208 to claim an inheritance and died on the journey, Geoffrey I of Villehardouin took control, and at the Parliament of Ravennika in 1209 he was recognised as a vassal of the <b>Latin Emperor Henry</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-achaea">Principality of Achaea · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Latin crusader forces under <b>Henry of Flanders</b> defeated an army of the Empire of Nicaea, led by Constantine Laskaris, at Adramyttion.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/march-19">19 March in history</a></li><li><blockquote>At the Rhyndacus, the Latin emperor <b>Henry of Flanders</b> defeated Theodore I Laskaris, founder of the Empire of Nicaea.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-15">15 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Alexius Slav allied with the Latin Empire of Constantinople, marrying a daughter of Emperor <b>Henry of Flanders</b>, and bore the title of despot.</blockquote><a href="/state/despotate-of-melnik">Despotate of Melnik</a></li><li><blockquote>Boniface was killed by the Bulgarians of Kaloyan in 1207, leaving his infant son Demetrius under a regency; the Lombard barons' revolt of 1208-1209 was suppressed by <b>Emperor Henry</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-thessalonica">Kingdom of Thessalonica</a></li><li><blockquote>His brother <b>Henry of Flanders</b> proved an able ruler, but after him the empire shrank to little more than the capital.</blockquote><a href="/state/latin-empire">Latin Empire</a></li></ul></section>
